## SECTION 14: FEATURED EXPERT

**expert_alias:** cameron-bennet

**expert_quote (full, verbatim from cluster_context.json):**
"Ingrown toenails can start without much pain before rapidly developing into something very sore. The common features of ingrown toenails are redness, swelling and pain. When the nail first starts pressing into the skin, it may or may not be painful and you might see a bit of callus (hard skin) forming around the nail edge. If that pressure continues, the nail can break through the skin and potentially introduce infection. This is where the skin surrounding the edge of the nail tends to become very sore to touch, quite red and inflamed, and you may even see pus coming from the ingrown edge."

